# Local run

Import Budget from "./budget.lg".
Import ChatRequest from "./chat_request.lg".
Import Conventions from "./conventions.lg".
Import HostFiles from "./host_files.lg".
Import Local from "./local.lg".
Import LocalPlan from "./local_plan.lg".
Import LocalSettings from "./local_settings.lg".
Import LocalStore from "./local_store.lg".
Import NodeRecord from "./node_record.lg".
Import Replay from "./replay.lg".

Up to a number of attempts on one problem, stopping at the first verified one, at
a budget stop, or when an attempt could not be made; and the two helpers that
let a person (or a test) answer the next prompt ahead of time as a recording.

## An Outcome has:
    a message, which is Text.
    an ok, which is Bool.

## To done (message: Text) -> Outcome:
    Return a new Outcome with message message and ok true.

## To failed (message: Text) -> Outcome:
    Return a new Outcome with message message and ok false.

## To runLocal (workspace: Text, problemId: Text, attempts: Int) -> Outcome:
    Inspect localSettings(workspace):
        When Err (e):
            Return failed(e).
        When Ok (s):
            Let mutable budget be newBudget(s's budgetMicros).
            Let mutable out be a new Seq of Text.
            Let mutable last be "".
            Let mutable going be true.
            While going and length of out is less than attempts:
                Let (o, b) be runAttempt(workspace, problemId, s, budget).
                Set budget to b.
                Push o's line to out.
                Set last to o's verdict.
                Set going to o's proceed.
            Push "spent " + formatMicros(budget's spentMicros) + " of " + formatMicros(budget's limitMicros) to out.
            If last is equal to "verified":
                Return done(join(out, "\n")).
            Return failed(join(out, "\n")).
    Return failed("unreachable").

## Note
A workspace holding the kernel fixture's statement (`0 + n = n`) as the accepted
statement of `local:zero_add`.

## To seedWorkspace (workspace: Text) -> Statement:
    Let doc be join(["/-! # Statement: zero is a left identity of addition on Nat", "", "Route C. A proof must establish `goal`. -/", "", "Definition goal : Prop := forall (n : Nat), Eq Nat (Nat_add Zero n) n."], "\n").
    Let mutable st be a new Statement with id ("stmt:" + sha256Hex(doc)) and problemId "local:zero_add" and document doc and sha256 sha256Hex(doc) and goalName "goal".
    Set st's route to "C".
    Set st's reviewState to "accepted".
    Set st's author to "fixture".
    Set st's model to "none".
    Let made be ensureDir(workspace + "/statements").
    Let w be writeText(workspace + "/statements/local_zero_add.json", toJson_Statement(st)).
    Return st.

## Note
The request the next attempt on `problemId` will make.

## To nextRequest (workspace: Text, problemId: Text) -> Result of ChatRequest and Text:
    Inspect loadStatement(workspace, problemId):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error e.
        When Ok (statement):
            Inspect loadTrail(workspace + "/trails/" + slugOf(problemId) + ".jsonl"):
                When Err (e):
                    Return a new Err with error e.
                When Ok (trail):
                    Return a new Ok with value planRequest(workspace, problemId, statement, trail, nextKind(trail)).
    Return a new Err with error "no request".

## Note
A recorded answer to the next attempt: the content a model would have sent, as a
reply costing `costMicros`. Answers the prompt hash.

## To answerNext (workspace: Text, problemId: Text, content: Text, costMicros: Int) -> Result of Text and Text:
    Inspect nextRequest(workspace, problemId):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error e.
        When Ok (request):
            Let reply be replyDocument("replay-" + promptSha(request), request's model, content, promptTokenBound(request), length of text_bytes(content), costMicros).
            Return recordReply(envOr("MACSAD_REPLAY_DIR", workspace + "/replays"), request, reply).
    Return a new Err with error "unanswered".
